# Maverick Wall — every variable, and every one optional.
#
# Copy to .env. A container started with none of these set works: it prints a
# setup code and shows the first-run wizard, which is the point.

# The address a browser will actually use to reach this.
#
# Defaults to http://localhost:<port>, and nobody browses to localhost from the
# sofa. If sign-in fails with "Missing or null Origin", this is why — the
# session cookie was set for somewhere the browser never goes. Set it to the
# address you type.
# BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.10:8080

# Where the calendar, settings and encryption key live. Inside the container
# this is /data and there is no reason to change it; mount a volume there.
# It must be absolute — a relative path resolves against the working directory,
# which is how one installation silently becomes two.
# DATA_DIR=/data

# The port inside the container. Change the left-hand side of the port mapping
# instead unless you have a reason.
# PORT=8080

# Where the wall's bundle is. Set by the image; only override if you are
# running from a checkout in an unusual layout.
# DISPLAY_DIR=/app/display

# Set by the Home Assistant supervisor when this runs as an add-on. Never set
# it yourself: its presence is how the application knows it is an add-on, and
# it is a credential with full control of the house.
# SUPERVISOR_TOKEN=

# Node's heap cap. 256MB is comfortable for a household calendar and means a
# leak restarts the container rather than having the kernel pick a victim.
# NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size=256
